                <pb facs="0237" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg129"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-02-12"><hi rendition="#italic">February 12, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received February 12.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson telegraphs that the insurgents on the preceding Saturday landed at
                    Nitcheroy and were repulsed, returning to their ships after an engagement, in
                    the course of which both sides lost heavily and Admiral da Gama received wounds
                    in his arm and breast.</p>
            </div>
